menu "WIFI 8711 (external Wi-Fi companion) module"

config WIFI_8711
	bool "External 8711 Wi-Fi chip over SPI"
	select SPI_AT_MASTER
	default n
	help
	  "An external 8711FA Wi-Fi companion exists."  Role-agnostic on
	  purpose: this is the symbol every Wi-Fi caller in app/protocol
	  (port_softap, port_tcp, jpgs_ingress, ebfs_ingress, cmd_debug) is
	  already guarded on, so it is what "pause the Wi-Fi features" turns
	  off -- each of those files has a working #else stub.

	  It selects SPI_AT_MASTER, which is the transport: WE drive SCLK and
	  CS and the 8711 runs Realtek's standard AT command set.  Turned on by
	  the wifi snippet, which also supplies the devicetree nodes that
	  transport binds to -- enabling the symbol on its own will not build.

	  It used to mean the SLAVE stack in app/wifi_8711/ instead.  That code
	  is now gated on WIFI_8711_ROLE_SLAVE (default n) rather than on this
	  symbol, because otherwise turning "an 8711 exists" on would compile a
	  module bound to spi0_slave, a node the wifi overlay does not provide.

config WIFI_8711_ROLE_SLAVE
	bool "SPI slave role (retired -- the custom-firmware stack)"
	depends on WIFI_8711
	select SPI
	select SPI_SLAVE
	default n
	help
	  Build app/wifi_8711/: the SPI slave transport plus the JPGS/ATMC slot
	  engine, talking to an 8711 running the CUSTOM in-house AT firmware
	  that understood the eBadge protocol.  The 8711 drove SCLK and CS and
	  we parked a 4096-byte slot in TX DMA waiting to be clocked.

	  RETIRED, and default n for two reasons rather than one: the standard
	  firmware replaced it, and the slave role capped the link at 10 MHz
	  where the master role reaches 25.  Kept buildable for bisecting
	  against known-good behaviour, not for shipping.

	  Needs the wifi_8711 snippet, not the wifi one -- it binds to
	  spi0_slave, and spi_rtl87x3g.c BUILD_ASSERTs that spi1 and spi1_hs
	  are not both okay, so the two overlays cannot be combined.

config WIFI_8711_TEST
	bool "wifi8711 shell command group"
	depends on WIFI_8711_ROLE_SLAVE && SHELL
	default n
	help
	  Register the `wifi8711` shell commands for the slave transport: probe
	  the DT bindings, drive the B2W line, and read W2B.

	  Depends on the ROLE_SLAVE symbol rather than on WIFI_8711, because
	  wifi_8711_shell.c lives in the module that symbol gates -- hanging it
	  off "an 8711 exists" would ask CMake for a source file the guard above
	  excluded.  The master role's equivalent is the `atm` group
	  (SPI_AT_MASTER_SHELL).

endmenu
